WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.066
I...

00:00:02.066 --> 00:00:04.066
dreamed about you once,

00:00:05.466 --> 00:00:08.066
before I even knew
you existed.

00:00:08.066 --> 00:00:09.826
Dreams are powerful omens.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.780
Perhaps we were
meant to find each other.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.733
Ciri really changes Yennefer.

00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:22.513
We see that, definitely at
the end of this Season.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.760
It is that moment of like,

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:25.680
ah this is Yennefer

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.360
because she spent the
entire season

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.733
with sort of hearing
bits and bobs,

00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:29.966
through Geralt

00:00:29.966 --> 00:00:31.533
and clearly, you know,
she's a smart girl,

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:32.940
she knows that...

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.240
she can sense she means
a lot to Geralt...

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.300
Who is Yennefer?

00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:42.000
and I think she's just excited
to find out more about her,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.633
and how they know
each other and everything.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.760
Obviously she’s given a huge clue
when she steps into that scene,

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.280
as to what their relationship is...

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.400
Geralt, do you know what
to do with this…

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:53.960
sorry.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:54.640
Ciri.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.880
And you know we’ve all been in
that kind of position

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.960
you know where you’re kind 
of like, sorry, oh my god,

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.800
 I’m so sorry, I’m gonna
leave now.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:01.760
Sorry…

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.280
You definitely have those
embarrassing moments,

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.960
where you’re like oh my god 
Dad is kissing someone!

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.933
Immediately in the
conversation where they're

00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:11.800
you know, surrounded by
the food and everything, 

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.533
in Melitele,

00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:15.033
I think Ciri's just taking in
the fact that she’s like,

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.500
clearly in front of another
very strong woman

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.366
who she admires.

00:01:18.366 --> 00:01:20.833
Anyone who’s any strong female

00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:22.633
is a reminder of her grandmother,

00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:25.193
and she always looked up to
the strength of her grandmother.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.433
I think she obviously sees that
in Yennefer instantly.

00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:31.313
Geralt says you’re the most
powerful mage he's ever known.

00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:33.900
Well that's nice of him.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.700
Ciri holds up a mirror to Yennefer

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.333
like no other character could,

00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:40.933
because she's got this
enormous amount of power

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:42.666
which she can't control,

00:01:42.666 --> 00:01:45.066
and that takes Yennefer right back

00:01:45.066 --> 00:01:46.700
to when she was 14 years old,

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.933
and Tissaia was teaching
her how to kind of

00:01:50.933 --> 00:01:52.373
hone this chaos.

00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:57.033
It is your job to control chaos,

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:57.900
not become it.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.380
I can.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.400
Yennefer sees in Ciri,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.800
kind of, Yennefer
as a child in Ciri,

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:09.033
and Ciri's struggles with trying to
understand her magic,

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:10.566
and what's inside her,

00:02:10.566 --> 00:02:12.400
and her identitiy, I suppose.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.000
As an orphan, like Yennefer,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.033
she can relate to that,

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:18.033
and because of that, she's
of great use to Ciri.

00:02:21.466 --> 00:02:23.226
Without, I think,
the relationship

00:02:23.233 --> 00:02:26.233
between Tissaia
and Yennefer,

00:02:26.233 --> 00:02:30.266
you wouldn't get the possibility
with Yennefer and Ciri.

00:02:30.266 --> 00:02:34.533
Yennefer meets Ciri and realises
she can be the same thing

00:02:34.533 --> 00:02:35.373
to Ciri.

00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:38.473
Use your knowledge of
magic to train the girl.

00:02:40.266 --> 00:02:42.666
You're the only person who's
helped to control her powers.

00:02:44.666 --> 00:02:46.900
When you have power like this

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.333
never apologise.

00:02:48.333 --> 00:02:50.466
One of her main issues
has been trusting

00:02:50.466 --> 00:02:53.733
I don't trust you.

00:02:53.733 --> 00:02:56.766
Especially after everything she's
experienced in Season 1,

00:02:56.766 --> 00:02:59.686
in regards to just meeting,
encountering, people on this continent

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.900
and how they
can be so brutal.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:02.833
I said stop.

00:03:02.833 --> 00:03:05.166
Our name is not Mousesack.

00:03:05.166 --> 00:03:07.466
But on top of that,
she’s also still this Season

00:03:07.466 --> 00:03:09.226
uncovering things about her family

00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:10.666
 and her background that she never knew,

00:03:10.666 --> 00:03:14.300
so she’s constantly got this
idea of lying and lack of trust,

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.300
and so I think it’s a big blow
when Yennefer does that,

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.300
it’s like another example of why

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.020
 I can’t trust anyone except
Geralt at this point, you know?

00:03:25.633 --> 00:03:27.300
 I had no choice.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.060
My chaos… I thought I had to…

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.066
 I think for Yennefer, the overriding
kind of emotion

00:03:35.066 --> 00:03:39.586
she goes to find Ciri with is just

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.320
I need to get my powers back

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:45.033
and she’s never kind of
hesitated before now

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:46.593
to get what she wants.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.800
And then when she’s with Ciri,
she just wants to save her.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.080
Trust your power to do the work.

00:03:55.233 --> 00:03:58.233
She realizes at the end of Season 2,

00:03:58.233 --> 00:04:00.433
that she’s willing to sacrifice herself

00:04:00.433 --> 00:04:02.473
to become a mother to Ciri.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:05.266
The relationship she forms with Ciri

00:04:05.266 --> 00:04:09.700
in the time that she’s taking her
on her journey to Voleth Meir -

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.600
Ciri just changes Yennefer’s
perspective on everything.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.333
I think the way that
Season 2 ended,

00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:18.213
obviously they did still create a bond.

00:04:18.233 --> 00:04:22.900
There’s this moment we established
where Geralt comes to them

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:23.633
in that scene,

00:04:23.633 --> 00:04:25.953
sort of implicates he has to kill a monster

00:04:25.953 --> 00:04:29.393
 and we played with the idea that she’s
wondering is he going to kill Yennefer.

00:04:29.986 --> 00:04:31.546
Where are you going?

00:04:32.433 --> 00:04:33.793
To slay a monster.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:36.533
Whatever Yennefer may have done,
she doesn’t want her to be killed.

00:04:36.533 --> 00:04:37.173
Say it.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.033
So there still is that connection
and it’s strong enough

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:43.240
 to maintain some kind of
like care for her in a way,

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.533
but it’s still going to be something

00:04:44.533 --> 00:04:47.000
 that needs to be worked through I believe.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.000
I’m intrigued to see how we
confront that in Season 3.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.760
Us three, we’ll help each other.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.400
What is destined cannot be avoided.

